      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        78.23609924316406,
        249.6569366455078,
        527.2255249023438,
        264.0999450683594
      ],
      "text": "Non-severe TB is defined as: Peripheral lymph node TB; intrathoracic lymph node TB without airway",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.961483001708984,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        82.86609649658203,
        262.8568115234375,
        527.6199951171875,
        277.2998352050781
      ],
      "text": "obstruction; uncomplicated TB pleural effusion or paucibacillary, non-cavitary disease, confined to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.991096496582031,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        82.86609649658203,
        276.05682373046875,
        324.503173828125,
        290.4998474121094
      ],
      "text": "one lobe of the lungs, and without a miliary pattern;",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        289.2568359375,
        78.23609924316406,
        303.6998596191406
      ],
      "text": "•",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        78.23609924316406,
        289.2568359375,
        527.2079467773438,
        303.6998596191406
      ],
      "text": "Children and adolescents who do not meet the criteria for non-severe TB should receive the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        82.86609649658203,
        302.456787109375,
        527.4322509765625,
        316.8998107910156
      ],
      "text": "standard six-month treatment regimen (2HRZE/4HR), or recommended treatment regimens for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        82.86609649658203,
        315.65692138671875,
        248.96945190429688,
        330.0999450683594
      ],
      "text": "severe forms of extrapulmonary TB.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        328.8568115234375,
        78.23609924316406,
        343.2998352050781
      ],
      "text": "•",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        78.23609924316406,
        328.8568115234375,
        527.1693725585938,
        343.2998352050781
      ],
      "text": "The use of ethambutol in the first two months of treatment is recommended in settings with a high",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.989595413208008,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        82.86609649658203,
        342.0567932128906,
        297.4998779296875,
        356.49981689453125
      ],
      "text": "prevalence of HIV , or of isoniazid resistance . 12 13",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        369.8741149902344,
        220.7113037109375,
        385.7261047363281
      ],
      "text": "Source of recommendation",
      "font": "SegoeUI-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        392.93402099609375,
        527.5896606445312,
        407.3770446777344
      ],
      "text": "This recommendation has been developed following advice from the Guidelines Development",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        406.1340026855469,
        527.4046630859375,
        420.5770263671875
      ],
      "text": "Group convened by the WHO Global Tuberculosis Programme in May-June 2021 on the topic of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        419.3340148925781,
        527.2164916992188,
        433.77703857421875
      ],
      "text": "the management of TB in children and adolescents. The recommendation is also featured in the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        432.53399658203125,
        495.3407897949219,
        446.9770202636719
      ],
      "text": "consolidated guidelines module on management of tuberculosis in children and adolescents.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        460.3512268066406,
        216.29168701171875,
        476.2032165527344
      ],
      "text": "Justification and evidence",
      "font": "SegoeUI-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        483.41119384765625,
        527.543701171875,
        497.8542175292969
      ],
      "text": "The majority of children with TB have less severe forms of the disease than adults. Treatment regimens",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.97652530670166,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        496.6112060546875,
        527.4585571289062,
        511.0542297363281
      ],
      "text": "that are shorter than those for adults may be effective in treating children with TB, however solid",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        509.81121826171875,
        527.55810546875,
        524.2542114257812
      ],
      "text": "evidence to substantiate this has been lacking to date. Shorter treatment regimens can result in lower",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.985940933227539,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        523.01123046875,
        527.4244384765625,
        537.4542236328125
      ],
      "text": "costs to families and health services, potentially less toxicity, lower risks of drug-drug interactions in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        536.2111206054688,
        527.4102783203125,
        550.6541137695312
      ],
      "text": "children living with HIV, and fewer problems with adherence. Shorter, safe and effective treatment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        549.4111938476562,
        527.3921508789062,
        563.8541870117188
      ],
      "text": "regimens for children with both drug-susceptible and DR-TB benefit children with TB and their families",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.967000961303711,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        562.6112060546875,
        527.4464721679688,
        577.05419921875
      ],
      "text": "and are a key intervention to achieve the WHO’s End TB Strategy targets, as well as targets related",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        575.8112182617188,
        527.4356689453125,
        590.2542114257812
      ],
      "text": "to children set during the UNGA HLM on TB in 2018. New evidence from a recently completed trial",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        589.01123046875,
        527.400390625,
        603.4542236328125
      ],
      "text": "on the shortened treatment of drug-susceptible TB in children and adolescents has paved the way",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        602.211181640625,
        355.5021667480469,
        616.6541748046875
      ],
      "text": "for new recommendations on shorter regimens for this group.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        623.9151000976562,
        527.4179077148438,
        638.3580932617188
      ],
      "text": "The SHINE trial (Shorter Treatment for Minimal Tuberculosis in Children) was the first and only large",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        637.1151123046875,
        527.3178100585938,
        651.55810546875
      ],
      "text": "phase three trial to evaluate the duration of TB treatment in children with non-severe drug-susceptible",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.967501640319824,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        650.3151245117188,
        527.4157104492188,
        664.7581176757812
      ],
      "text": "TB. Therefore, evidence from the trial rather than a systematic review, was used to answer this",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        662.2391357421875,
        527.38916015625,
        677.9581298828125
      ],
      "text": "(35) PICO question  . The SHINE trial was a multi-centre, open-label, parallel-group, non-inferiority,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        676.715087890625,
        524.5060424804688,
        691.1580810546875
      ],
      "text": "randomized, controlled, two-arm trial comparing four-month (16 weeks) versus the standard six-",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        689.9151000976562,
        527.1481323242188,
        704.3580932617188
      ],
      "text": "month (24 weeks) treatment durations in children under 16 years of age with symptomatic non-severe",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.968655586242676,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        718.2369995117188,
        526.598388671875,
        731.9409790039062
      ],
      "text": "Defined as countries, subnational administrative units, or selected facilities, where the HIV prevalence among adult pregnant women is  12",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        730.1090087890625,
        526.6806640625,
        741.541015625
      ],
      "text": "Guidance for national tuberculosis programmes on the management of tuberculosis in children  ≥1% or among TB patients is ≥5% in the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 7.999749660491943,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        739.708984375,
        153.95468139648438,
        751.1409912109375
      ],
      "text": "(second edition)  2014.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        749.8717041015625,
        526.570556640625,
        763.57568359375
      ],
      "text": "WHO does not intend to establish thresholds for low, moderate or high levels of prevalence of isoniazid resistance: NTPs will establish  13",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
